<article class="env-lemma" id="0G8D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G8D">Lemma <span data-tag="0G8D">50.23.10</span>.</a> Let $c \geq 0$ and </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ Z' \ar[d]_ h \ar[r] &  X' \ar[d]_ g \ar[r] &  S' \ar[d] \\  Z \ar[r] &  X \ar[r] &  S }  \]
</div>
  <p> satisfy the assumptions of Lemma <a href="/tag/0G89" data-tag="0G89">50.23.6</a> and assume in addition that $X \to S$ and $X' \to S'$ are smooth and that $Z \to X$ and $Z' \to X'$ are Koszul regular immersions. Then the diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ H^ q(Z, \Omega ^ p_{Z/S}) \ar[rr]_-{\gamma ^{p, q}} \ar[d] &  &  H^{q + c}(X, \Omega ^{p + c}_{X/S}) \ar[d] \\  H^ q(Z', \Omega ^ p_{Z'/S'}) \ar[rr]^{\gamma ^{p, q}} &  &  H^{q + c}(X', \Omega ^{p + c}_{X'/S'}) }  \]
</div>
  <p> is commutative where $\gamma ^{p, q}$ is as in Remark <a href="/tag/0G8A" data-tag="0G8A">50.23.7</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows on combining Lemma <a href="/tag/0G89" data-tag="0G89">50.23.6</a> and Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0G79" data-tag="0G79">20.34.13</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>